[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b1: empirical, bias-informed null model
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   Step 02 tested the detached-TNO clustering against a conditioned
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   null in which om and w are drawn uniform on the circle.  That null
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   is unrealistic: real surveys point at specific ecliptic longitudes,
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   objects are found near opposition and near their nodes, and
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   eccentric objects are found preferentially near perihelion (step 06
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   measured this directly in OSSOS: mean |varpi - lam_d| = 51 deg,
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   R_coupling = 0.513).
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   This step replaces the uniform angular null with an *empirical*
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   one built from the catalog itself, and then asks how much
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   perihelion-proximity coupling would be required to manufacture the
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   observed signal.
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   E1  Control-resample null.  The ~1200-object control population
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   (30 < a <= 150 AU, q > 30, cc <= 3, arc > 200 d) carries the
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   real angular discovery filter: its (om, w) joint distribution
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   encodes nodal bias, opposition geometry, and ecliptic-pointing
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   structure.  For each MC realization the detached sample keeps
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   its observed (a, e, i) and draws (om, w) pairs -- jointly, to
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   preserve their correlation -- from the control pool.  Any
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   clustering the filter itself produces is now inside the null.
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   E2  Perihelion-proximity augmentation sweep.  The control pool
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   under-represents one channel: detached objects, being distant
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   and faint, are found much closer to perihelion than the
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   controls.  An object found near perihelion near the ecliptic
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   has w ~ 0 or 180 deg, so varpi ~ om and the perihelion
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   direction inherits the footprint longitude.  A fraction f of
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   the null objects is therefore drawn from a "found near
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   perihelion" component: om from the control footprint,
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   w ~ von Mises(0 or 180, kappa).  The sweep in f asks: at what
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   coupling strength does the bias reproduce the observed
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   R(varpi) = 0.33?  The OSSOS coupling (step 06: effective
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   biased fraction ~ 0.4) marks the empirically calibrated point.
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   E3  Direct OSSOS calibration.  The OSSOS detached objects' own
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   (om, w, varpi, lam_d) joint is used to estimate the biased
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   fraction and its angular spread, giving an empirical anchor
[2026-09-20 10:42:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 013]   for the E2 sweep rather than an assumed one.
